{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508147-why-the-world-of-darkness-god-gave-cain-so-much-priviliges","id":1508147,"title":"Why the World of Darkness God gave Cain so much priviliges?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-04-12T06:45:56-07:00","id":1508147,"title":"Why the World of Darkness God gave Cain so much priviliges?","content":"In the WoD main story, Cain murdered his own brother and is utterly unrepentant about it. God offers him every occasion to repent, even giving him eternal life and sending three ( or four according to the Golconda legend ) angels to offer him forgiveness.<br /> <br /> A common vampire Embraced against his will, who's worse sins were lying to his wife and cursing after a disliked politician, can pray and beg and cry and repent as much as he wants but 99% of time Heaven stay absolutely silent to his prayers and no angel is there to offer any kind of salvation.<br /> <br /> So...<br /> why?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","name":"Conradine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8595_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-12T10:10:01-07:00","id":1508158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Conradine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508147-why-the-world-of-darkness-god-gave-cain-so-much-priviliges#post1508147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the WoD main story, Cain murdered his own brother and is utterly unrepentant about it. God offers him every occasion to repent, even giving him eternal life and sending three ( or four according to the Golconda legend ) angels to offer him forgiveness.<br /> <br /> A common vampire Embraced against his will, who's worse sins were lying to his wife and cursing after a disliked politician, can pray and beg and cry and repent as much as he wants but 99% of time Heaven stay absolutely silent to his prayers and no angel is there to offer any kind of salvation.<br /> <br /> So...<br /> why?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Because the WOD god is basically the biblical god.<br /> <br /> He has strange fixations on specific individuals, no small ammount of crueltyand don't hesidate to cause suffering for innocents that happens to be in the way.<br /> <br /> Look at the story of Job. Just for the sake of a bet with the Accuser, he made his life a living hell, and didn't hesitated to kill Job's children to cause him despair for said bet.<br /> <br /> So his behavior with Caine is pretty on point. He's as much petty to others if we trust both Lilith's account and Demon the fallen's lore.<br /> <br /> <br /> A possible counterpoint is that the angels only came after Lilith started to awaken Caine. So it may be that god tried to avoid Caine becoming as powerful as her.<br /> Which is also a typical genesis like narrative (like the whole angel with a flaming sword stopping humans from obtaining the fruits of the tree of life).<br /> <br /> Also, a third point about angels noy coming to help truly repentant people is that God is either dead or leaved creation according to some lore<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-12T10:52:23-07:00","id":1508163,"title":"","content":"Potential answers I came up with on the spot:<br /> <br /> 1) The WoD's god is a narcissistic dick.<br /> <br /> 2) Said god died or otherwise fell out of reach sometime after the events of the Book of Nod.<br /> <br /> 3) It's just Noddist propaganda. There were no angels offering forgiveness in the first place. Perhaps the whole Cainite origin is a sham (ToJ scenarios all seem to be AU to each other)<br /> <br /> 4) At the very least, perhaps events did not unfold as stated. Perhaps the being who created vampirism isn't actually powerful enough to undo the curse anyway - or didn't create it in the first place.<br /> <br /> 5) Due to some fine print in the curse, the curse cannot be removed from the higher generations unless it's removed from the goddamned deadbeat father of all vampires by his saying he's sorry. Caine is the linchpin holding the curse in existence, if he's still a vampire, we're all still vampires.<br /> <br /> 6) Vampires are part of the plan for the WoD, and god doesn't want the curse lifted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-12T11:34:28-07:00","id":1508169,"title":"","content":"My theory is that God didn't. For various obvious reasons, it doesn't make sense why God would grant Caine all these vampire powers so he could torment the rest of mankind (after explicitly punishing Caine for murder in the first place). God did not make Caine a vampire. The Noddists are wrong in that.<br /> <br /> The Lilins are correct that &quot;Lilith&quot; (whatever she might be) is who bestowed vampirism upon Caine. Presumably Caine, because he is a giant murderous ass, wanted to become a vampire (though he may not have understood all the implications of that) because he wanted to get back at God, and was the one who approached Lilith and made whatever deal was necessary to do so. However, the Lilins are wrong that they think &quot;Lilith&quot; was the first vampire. Caine was still the first vampire (in terms of generation). Whatever Lilith was, she wasn't the first vampire, but she was the mystic source of whatever allowed Caine to turn into a vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":". 04-12-2023, 02:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-12T12:35:11-07:00","id":1508174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Conradine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508147-why-the-world-of-darkness-god-gave-cain-so-much-priviliges#post1508147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the WoD main story, Cain murdered his own brother and is utterly unrepentant about it. God offers him every occasion to repent, even giving him eternal life and sending three ( or four according to the Golconda legend ) angels to offer him forgiveness.<br /> <br /> A common vampire Embraced against his will, who's worse sins were lying to his wife and cursing after a disliked politician, can pray and beg and cry and repent as much as he wants but 99% of time Heaven stay absolutely silent to his prayers and no angel is there to offer any kind of salvation.<br /> <br /> So...<br /> why?</div> </div> </div> </div>Who is to say that the Book of Nod, Lilith or the Eneryies Fragments are being completely truthful at all?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-12T12:56:41-07:00","id":1508180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Conradine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508147-why-the-world-of-darkness-god-gave-cain-so-much-priviliges#post1508147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So...<br /> why?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's mythology. It's a set of stories vampires tell themselves to explain their existence, and if anyone knows the whole truth of what really happened in the WoD, they haven't actually bothered offering a history of vampires instead. The Noddist mythology focuses on Caine because of a mixture of their own biases, and because the nature of WoD vampires to go back to one progenitor vampire - with each generation of vampires increasingly more powerful the closer you get to the original - means you need to explain how the first is exactly that powerful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-12T14:57:24-07:00","id":1508198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508147-why-the-world-of-darkness-god-gave-cain-so-much-priviliges?p=1508169#post1508169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My theory is that God didn't. For various obvious reasons, it doesn't make sense why God would grant Caine all these vampire powers so he could torment the rest of mankind (after explicitly punishing Caine for murder in the first place). God did not make Caine a vampire. The Noddists are wrong in that.<br /> <br /> The Lilins are correct that &quot;Lilith&quot; (whatever she might be) is who bestowed vampirism upon Caine. Presumably Caine, because he is a giant murderous ass, wanted to become a vampire (though he may not have understood all the implications of that) because he wanted to get back at God, and was the one who approached Lilith and made whatever deal was necessary to do so. However, the Lilins are wrong that they think &quot;Lilith&quot; was the first vampire. Caine was still the first vampire (in terms of generation). Whatever Lilith was, she wasn't the first vampire, but she was the mystic source of whatever allowed Caine to turn into a vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> To be fair, most of the vampiric powers, according to the book of nod, don't come from the angels' curses. <br /> <br /> From the angels, all he gained is undeath and the ability to feed on blood, as positive consequences of the curses laid upon him.<br /> <br /> The rest of his powers comes from the ritual that he went through thanks to Lilith.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-12T15:10:57-07:00","id":1508199,"title":"","content":"Depends on who you ask. Firstly it's not exactly clear what happened since we're going of Caines account. Furthermore days of fire implies their we're serious metaphysical consequences of the first murder which go way beyond a contemporary bad thing.<br /> <br /> I also wouldn't really consider eternal life in that context a blessing","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-12T15:22:06-07:00","id":1508200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Conradine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508147-why-the-world-of-darkness-god-gave-cain-so-much-priviliges#post1508147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the WoD main story, Cain murdered his own brother and is utterly unrepentant about it. God offers him every occasion to repent, even giving him eternal life and sending three ( or four according to the Golconda legend ) angels to offer him forgiveness.<br /> <br /> A common vampire Embraced against his will, who's worse sins were lying to his wife and cursing after a disliked politician, can pray and beg and cry and repent as much as he wants but 99% of time Heaven stay absolutely silent to his prayers and no angel is there to offer any kind of salvation.<br /> <br /> So...<br /> why?</div> </div> </div> </div>Cause God in the World of Darkness is an inconsistent messy bitch who is not there to make things better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-12T15:45:07-07:00","id":1508201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508147-why-the-world-of-darkness-god-gave-cain-so-much-priviliges?p=1508169#post1508169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My theory is that God didn't. For various obvious reasons, it doesn't make sense why God would grant Caine all these vampire powers so he could torment the rest of mankind (after explicitly punishing Caine for murder in the first place). God did not make Caine a vampire. The Noddists are wrong in that.<br /> <br /> The Lilins are correct that &quot;Lilith&quot; (whatever she might be) is who bestowed vampirism upon Caine. Presumably Caine, because he is a giant murderous ass, wanted to become a vampire (though he may not have understood all the implications of that) because he wanted to get back at God, and was the one who approached Lilith and made whatever deal was necessary to do so. However, the Lilins are wrong that they think &quot;Lilith&quot; was the first vampire. Caine was still the first vampire (in terms of generation). Whatever Lilith was, she wasn't the first vampire, but she was the mystic source of whatever allowed Caine to turn into a vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>This has always been my stance. The importance of the Caine monomyth has been overblown. He may have been the first, but he was not necessarily the most important being in the history of time with more attention from God by anyone else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-12T16:03:38-07:00","id":1508204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508147-why-the-world-of-darkness-god-gave-cain-so-much-priviliges?p=1508201#post1508201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This has always been my stance. The importance of the Caine monomyth has been overblown. He may have been the first, but he was not necessarily the most important being in the history of time with more attention from God by anyone else.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a bit harder to legitamize that stance when about 50% of the metaplot and the entirety of ghenna focus reinforce the noddist perspective.<br /> <br /> The writers basically declared the &quot;Caine&quot; version of events canon when they originally ended WoD, and 20th doesn't really backtrack that on that so much as say STs don't have to go with it(while also adding more noddist elements).<br /> <br /> Things are even messier with V5, because the 5th edition set is breaking away from and soft-rebooting aspects of the franchise. So Arguments change drastically between editions. It might be good to clarify which edition one holds their stance for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-12T16:08:04-07:00","id":1508205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508147-why-the-world-of-darkness-god-gave-cain-so-much-priviliges?p=1508204#post1508204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's a bit harder to legitamize that stance when about 50% of the metaplot and the entirety of ghenna focus reinforce the noddist perspective.<br /> <br /> The writers basically declared the &quot;Caine&quot; version of events canon when they originally ended WoD, and 20th doesn't really backtrack that on that so much as say STs don't have to go with it(while also adding more noddist elements).<br /> <br /> Things are even messier with V5, because the 5th edition set is breaking away from and soft-rebooting aspects of the franchise. So Arguments change drastically between editions. It might be good to clarify which edition one holds their stance for.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gehenna didn't really prove anything, considering it's a buffet of options rather than a conclusive proof of anything. Caine was irrelevant to most of the written endings. And as much as people like to claim Vampire is the be-and-all of WoD, the other ending books didn't see Caine or the whole Christianity fixation very relevant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-12T16:33:55-07:00","id":1508208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508147-why-the-world-of-darkness-god-gave-cain-so-much-priviliges?p=1508205#post1508205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Gehenna didn't really prove anything, considering it's a buffet of options rather than a conclusive proof of anything. Caine was irrelevant to most of the written endings. And as much as people like to claim Vampire is the be-and-all of WoD, the other ending books didn't see Caine or the whole Christianity fixation very relevant.</div> </div> </div> </div>Casually forgetting demon the fallen I see.<br /> <br /> But joking aside, the other game-lines don't matter. We moved away from the &quot;One world of Darkness&quot; thing in revised. What happened in VTM has nothing to do with WTA or Mage, barring explicit exceptions like the week of nightmares or umbra storm(Because WoD loves its exceptions.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-12T16:44:26-07:00","id":1508212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508147-why-the-world-of-darkness-god-gave-cain-so-much-priviliges?p=1508208#post1508208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Casually forgetting demon the fallen I see.<br /> <br /> But joking aside, the other game-lines don't matter. We moved away from the &quot;One world of Darkness&quot; thing in revised. What happened in VTM has nothing to do with WTA or Mage, barring explicit exceptions like the week of nightmares or umbra storm(Because WoD loves its exceptions.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Ehh. When 20th edition lines describe the other splats they describe the actual splats, often describing factions and clans/tribes/traditions/kith/blah directly. There's a building in Stygia named for a Giovanni vampire, Changeling directly references the Triat and WtA cosmology in the Thallain writeup (&quot;Gaia's Mercy&quot;, &quot;Hatred of the Weaver&quot;, &quot;Curse of the Weaver&quot;)<br /> <br /> There's still plenty of room to consider it one joint world if one wants to, imo","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-12T16:44:47-07:00","id":1508213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508147-why-the-world-of-darkness-god-gave-cain-so-much-priviliges?p=1508205#post1508205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And as much as people like to claim Vampire is the be-and-all of WoD, the other ending books didn't see Caine or the whole Christianity fixation very relevant.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've long considered &quot;Caine&quot; to simply be the placeholder for &quot;first vampire&quot;, and that is pretty much all that is really known about him. The patina of Biblical lore about him is mostly because the last 1500+ plus years have been dominated by the Abrahamic monotheistic religions. People don't like the unknown, and therefore they fill in the blank spaces with things they do know. Likewise &quot;Lilith&quot; could be any number of evil spirits of darkness. Prior to the rise of Christianity, vampires probably filled in the unknown with concepts that made sense to them. Only the Antedeluvians would truly know, and we don't know what they actually told their childer or how their childer would have interpreted what they were told.<br /> <br /> If you boil down the basic myth of Vampire to its essentials, you have the concept of 1) there was a world before this one, 2) the origins of vampirism can be found in that previous world, 3) that previous world was destroyed, and 4) there were some vampire survivors of that previous world that are the progenitors of all vampires today.<br /> <br /> That previous world could have been the pre-Deluge world of the Bible, or it could be Atlantis, Numenor, or the Hyborian Age among many other alternatives. The first vampire could be Caine, or it might be Varnae of Marvel Comics, some servant of Sauron, Princess Akivasha of the Hyborian Age, or something else. Lilith might be Lilith, Hecate, Tiamat, Nyaralthotep, Sauron, the Great Serpent, or anything else. Was it the Flood of Noah, Deucalion, Utnapishtim, the sinking of Atlantis, or the Hyborian Cataclysm that destroyed the previous world?<br /> <br /> Having one or the other be true doesn't actually change the setting at all. Likewise, some of the other gamelines have invented their own understanding of the origins of vampirism, and they are usually presented in a way that makes just as much sense in the greater setting as the official Noddist line. Not to mention even within Vampire, some clans do have an alternative version of events.<br /> <br /> There's no problem with wanting the Abrahamic version to be the explicit truth. It makes good gothic horror. But it is not the only possible origin that would make sense, and an ST can decide whatever they wanted - but such specifics likely won't matter at all unless the ST is actually running an actual Gehenna scenario in their chronicles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-12T16:55:57-07:00","id":1508215,"title":"","content":"Honestly I always interpreted Caine, if he exists, as actually being <i>alive</i>. Blessed with immortality so he may find the time to repent, cursed with a thirst for blood, and having developed strange powers that became the vampiric Disciplines and let him spread his condition to the recently dead, but personally still among the living.<br /> <br /> Also him being Caine is probably just Abrahamic kindred slapping their religion on everything.<br /> <br /> Thus the reason he gets to repent and nobody else does is because a truly remorseful kindred would find a way to kill themselves. At that point they'd be judged to their beliefs and their deeds, including their mortal life and their battle against the Beast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-12T19:40:28-07:00","id":1508233,"title":"","content":"I have always found odd how VtM writers tried to push an extremely specific religious vision into the lore and how a legend ended up becoming canon instead of just a story Kindred tell themselves in an attempt to make sense of their existence.<br /> I have moved away from that &quot;canon&quot; in my games and established that Cainite lore and the biblical curse interpretation of vampirism it only appeared around the time of Rome as an underground movement opposed to the &quot;classical&quot; legend that viewed vampires as children of the gods. <br /> Obviously this is Masquerade and not Requiem, and the way generation works strongly suggest an original first Vampire. But how they came to be can be explained in many different ways, including a curse, a deal, a powerful sorcery ritual...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","name":"Microcuchon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-12T20:13:18-07:00","id":1508237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508147-why-the-world-of-darkness-god-gave-cain-so-much-priviliges?p=1508205#post1508205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Gehenna didn't really prove anything, considering it's a buffet of options rather than a conclusive proof of anything. Caine was irrelevant to most of the written endings. And as much as people like to claim Vampire is the be-and-all of WoD, the other ending books didn't see Caine or the whole Christianity fixation very relevant.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> gehenna, regardless of the scenario, a knowledge the noddist mythology as true.<br /> <br /> The abrahamic god run out of patience with caine in the first scenario, the second is about caine facing lilith, the third has saulot taking the mentle of dead caine to ask an angel for forgiveness for the cainites, and in tte end of the fourth, god literally mock a desesperate caine wishing for an end to his torment.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for the rest of the WOD, it doesn't matter. Everyone who opened two books from two different WOD game knows that the author didn't even tried to create a unified cosmology, so unless said cosmology works alongside vampire, like wraith or demon, they don't really matter to the discussion<br /> \u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-12T20:14:52-07:00","id":1508238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Microcuchon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508147-why-the-world-of-darkness-god-gave-cain-so-much-priviliges?p=1508233#post1508233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have always found odd how VtM writers tried to push an extremely specific religious vision into the lore and how a legend ended up becoming canon instead of just a story Kindred tell themselves in an attempt to make sense of their existence.<br /> I have moved away from that &quot;canon&quot; in my games and established that Cainite lore and the biblical curse interpretation of vampirism it only appeared around the time of Rome as an underground movement opposed to the &quot;classical&quot; legend that viewed vampires as children of the gods.<br /> Obviously this is Masquerade and not Requiem, and the way generation works strongly suggest an original first Vampire. But how they came to be can be explained in many different ways, including a curse, a deal, a powerful sorcery ritual...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> i wonder why you find it odd. Many games have a canon origin story that is wrapped in myth. The authors never claimed to wish for a nebulous origin story with many possibilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-12T21:00:44-07:00","id":1508245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508147-why-the-world-of-darkness-god-gave-cain-so-much-priviliges?p=1508238#post1508238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <br /> i wonder why you find it odd. Many games have a canon origin story that is wrapped in myth. The authors never claimed to wish for a nebulous origin story with many possibilities.</div> </div> </div> </div> I started playing Masquerade 1st edition back in 1991. In page 29 of that book you have the 1st reference to the book of nod and the curse of Caine. <br /> Before a two pages long extract from the Book of Nod, we are warned that nobody knows whether this story is real or invented and that Anarchs reject it. Considering Anarchs are almost the default faction in 1st edition, the implication is clear: this is most likely a lie. Actually, one of Masquerade's main themes is that lies and deception are a powerful tool of control. <br /> So, imagine my disappointment when, as more and more products are added to the game line, we find out that, according to canon, everything we were told in page 29 of the first book was, exactly and unequivocally, THE TRUTH. Quite a way to shoot yourself in the foot thematically. <br /> Additionally, I dislike that is the biblical story that's true. Christians may be the largest religious denomination in today's world, but they are barely 1/3. If we add Muslims and other groups who believe in the Abrahamic God you can make it to 50%. But they happen to be right. <br /> In conclusion: the &quot;Elders are actually right, monotheists are actually right&quot; sounds anticlimactic and antithematic to me. <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","name":"Microcuchon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-12T21:48:31-07:00","id":1508248,"title":"","content":"Nobody knows for certain what the truth is. We only know for certain as far as Antediluvians are true. The rest almost doesn't really influence the story at al. <br /> The Gehenna scenarios were terrible in my opinion, they utterly destroyed that which was one of the most important pillars of Vampire, that is its mystery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-12T23:06:42-07:00","id":1508249,"title":"","content":"The increased presence of Noddist lore in the games, and even the Gehenna end scenarios, don't prove the Noddist myths were true. It just explained what they were in more detail, and maybe they got some things right. There were whole other myths published at that time. The idea that Noddists were made canonically correct is far more fanon<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-13T00:14:44-07:00","id":1508251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Conradine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508147-why-the-world-of-darkness-god-gave-cain-so-much-priviliges#post1508147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> In the WoD main story, Cain murdered his own brother and is utterly unrepentant about it. God offers him every occasion to repent, even giving him eternal life and sending three ( or four according to the Golconda legend ) angels to offer him forgiveness.<br /> <br /> A common vampire Embraced against his will, who's worse sins were lying to his wife and cursing after a disliked politician, can pray and beg and cry and repent as much as he wants but 99% of time Heaven stay absolutely silent to his prayers and no angel is there to offer any kind of salvation.<br /> <br /> So...<br /> why?</div> </div> </div> </div>One way to answer this question is to consider that Cain and Abel ( and other persons and beings in the area ) had prior dealings with this spirit being that is referred to as &quot;God&quot; . Hence the attention and actions of this supernatural being towards Cain, and later also interactions with Angels.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Conradine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508147-why-the-world-of-darkness-god-gave-cain-so-much-priviliges#post1508147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">can pray and beg and cry and repent as much as he wants but 99% of time Heaven stay absolutely silent to his prayers and no angel is there to offer any kind of salvation.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is actually a real chance or option of an intervention or activity of a mystical being or a supernatural person ( or a group of them ) ; as a reaction to this. The chances and the possible events can vary depending on decisions, choices, ideas, qualities and circumstances.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508147-why-the-world-of-darkness-god-gave-cain-so-much-priviliges?p=1508169#post1508169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Lilins are correct that &quot;Lilith&quot; (whatever she might be) is who bestowed vampirism upon Caine.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is entirely correct. Lilith is the saviour and the tempter responsible for this occurence. Assuming it can be considered and looked upon is such simple terms.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508147-why-the-world-of-darkness-god-gave-cain-so-much-priviliges?p=1508169#post1508169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whatever Lilith was, she wasn't the first vampire, but she was the mystic source of whatever allowed Caine to turn into a vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as I am aware, Lilith is a Mage. In some Mage: the Ascension books, supplements and guides Lilith is listed as one of the Wyck - powerful, wise, cunning, and intelligent witches or sorceresses.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-13T01:22:47-07:00","id":1508254,"title":"","content":"It does kinda feel like the Noddist origin became canon. Or at least the Noddists hold a large chunk of the truth, if they're not 100% correct. <br /> The problem is that the editions don't stick with a single answer about the nature of the setting/s and accuracy of Noddism.<br /> <br /> VtM started off with it just being a story.<br /> <br /> Time of Judgement treats the lines as separate universes, in which VtM is Abrahamic fiction and Noddism is fact.<br /> <br /> And then 20th treats things as a more flexible joint setting where the ToJ need not apply.<br /> <br /> In the opening fiction of Wr20 we get the line &quot;Their father killed ours&quot; (ie, Cain and Abel), Giovanni and Lasombra are both mentioned as part of Wraith world building to confirm that, yes, we're talking VtM... and then the book explains that the Pandemonium arcanos was created by the Wyld from WtA. We've got at least one setting that acknowledges two other gamelines with conflicting cosmologies as true and sharing a setting with it.<br /> <br /> Changeling also supports the fratricide angle, though not the Abrahamic lore of it. A fairy born of dreams of violence and fear murdered his brother and became a vampire, or else they descend from Lilith - who in this version is a fairy born of primeval nightmares who gets banished from the Dreaming along with the rest of her lineage.<br /> Changeling acknowledges Vtm, Noddist lore and WtA and the Triat.<br /> <br /> Wr20 and C20 explicitly, in their own lore, cohabit a setting with both V20 and W20, and by extension M20. 1/5 of WoD20 largely goes with an Abrahamic backstory. 1/5 rejects it. 1/5 is vague and 2/5 state the world doesn't have a concrete setting because it's shaped by stories and belief. It seems more like a case where everyone has a fragment of truth, but it's not thhe whole story. (That Malkavian story about the vampire bats and the elephant spring to mind)<br /> <br /> What seems to be &quot;factual&quot; in the WoD(20) is that some idiot killed his brother and invented vampires, some exiled being called &quot;Lilith&quot; who doesn't belong to any of the splats was involved, and the Metaphysical Trinity definitely exists. The accuracy of the religious bent of Noddism and the nature of divinity in the WoD is more open to questioning.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-13T02:09:38-07:00","id":1508262,"title":"","content":"I found the Caine myth to be interesting out of the aspect that it was so human. In many ways it really felt like Kindred tried to cram in a modern christian myth to make sense of the world. It justified both themselves and their mortal religion.<br /> But there is a clear lack of alternative stories, that stand in conflict, which is something I think that would add to the myths rather than subtract, even though the complexity increases.<br /> <br /> That it would actually be true seemed a bit foreign, in particular in light of the other game lines. While Demon eventually took the sort of side of Abrahamic religions, most memories of the Demons were from the point of view of possessing someone with an already defined image of what god, angels and demons were, making them the very definition of unreliable narrators. <br /> <br /> In a game I ran, there was a coven (I misremember the actual names, kamut?) of Black Hand Noddists that questioned the Caine myth. During conversation with players they openly discussed that the usage of the word Caine was a first millennium, and the original words that had been translated to Caine was more of \u201cthe first\u201d, \u201cthe eldest\u201d or \u201cthe father\u201d or simply other similar names to that context, making many modern translations full of contradictions. Still, they agreed that Caine was as good name as any, and never brought up texts that challenged the view that there would not be an original vampire, like the good zealous scholars they were.<br /> <br /> In my own head canon I have never made up my mind, but it\u2019s either a long dead original vampire, or what is referred to as the Antediluvians are all original vampires, commiting various sins or rituals that bestowed them vampirism, in an age where magic flowed more natural, setting the earths rules for undeath at the same time.<br /> Either way, it would simply not matter, because age and myth could weave any stories of it, and none of the original actors would interact with the players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12225-trassel","name":"Trassel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-13T13:24:04-07:00","id":1508293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Microcuchon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508147-why-the-world-of-darkness-god-gave-cain-so-much-priviliges?p=1508245#post1508245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I started playing Masquerade 1st edition back in 1991. In page 29 of that book you have the 1st reference to the book of nod and the curse of Caine.<br /> Before a two pages long extract from the Book of Nod, we are warned that nobody knows whether this story is real or invented and that Anarchs reject it. Considering Anarchs are almost the default faction in 1st edition, the implication is clear: this is most likely a lie. Actually, one of Masquerade's main themes is that lies and deception are a powerful tool of control.<br /> So, imagine my disappointment when, as more and more products are added to the game line, we find out that, according to canon, everything we were told in page 29 of the first book was, exactly and unequivocally, THE TRUTH. Quite a way to shoot yourself in the foot thematically.<br /> Additionally, I dislike that is the biblical story that's true. Christians may be the largest religious denomination in today's world, but they are barely 1/3. If we add Muslims and other groups who believe in the Abrahamic God you can make it to 50%. But they happen to be right.<br /> In conclusion: the &quot;Elders are actually right, monotheists are actually right&quot; sounds anticlimactic and antithematic to me.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It seems then that your disappointment comes from reading too much from one sentence.<br /> <br /> &quot;We're not sure if the story is true and anarch believe it's made up for control&quot; simply speaks of the lacj of definitive proof for the myth of nod, and of the mistrust of anarchs toward it. <br /> <br /> <br /> Also, remember that 1st ed corebooks were, at most, sketchbooks of the games. Mage the ascebsuon 1st corebook is basically a wholly different game compared to what mage become following that book.<br /> <br /> So the abarch centrist viewpoint only existed for a few books.<br /> <br /> Also &quot;christians are only x percent of the world&quot;, doesn't matter. Unless you dive too deep in mage's cosmology.<br /> <br /> In all urban fantasy, there's a real truth behind supernaturals being, either as species, like in the WOD, or englobing all of them. And this truth cab align with some real life beliefs. Which means others are wrong.<br /> <br /> And it's not a problem, you don't need to care about every beliefs of the world to creates your urban fantasy worldbuilding.<br /> <br /> Also, VTM doesn't really confirm monotheism. In fact, the whole &quot;testament of Lilith&quot; thing contradicts it.<br /> <br /> All that is certain, is that a god baniqhed a couple from Eden, and Lilith before them, and that he cursed their eldest son for killing his brother.<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> And that's all. The nature of that god is left pretty unknown, and even adding Demon the fallen's lore into all that, the god described, while clearly inspired from the abrahamic god, is pretty different from said god.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bAs for the theme of lies and manipulation through use of myths, it is respected by the fact that, at least since 2nd edition, the camarilla denied the reality of the myrh of Nod because they want to control the younglings.<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> \u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-13T13:27:16-07:00","id":1508294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508147-why-the-world-of-darkness-god-gave-cain-so-much-priviliges?p=1508248#post1508248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nobody knows for certain what the truth is. We only know for certain as far as Antediluvians are true. The rest almost doesn't really influence the story at al.<br /> The Gehenna scenarios were terrible in my opinion, they utterly destroyed that which was one of the most important pillars of Vampire, that is its mystery.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Gehenna was literally an end of the world book, it was THE moment to reveal the truth. Mystery can only last for so long, and the gameline was ending.<br /> <br /> <br /> And there's still mystery. While the truth of Caine is set in these books, most of the background stays in shadows.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-13T13:41:05-07:00","id":1508297,"title":"","content":"I always went with the notion that all three books contained bits of the truth mixed in with lies and mistakes as they have told and retold so many times.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-13T16:49:35-07:00","id":1508308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508147-why-the-world-of-darkness-god-gave-cain-so-much-priviliges?p=1508297#post1508297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always went with the notion that all three books contained bits of the truth mixed in with lies and mistakes as they have told and retold so many times.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's indeed pretty much cabon that some elder, notably Saulot, modified it to make him appears better and to advance gehenna","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-13T19:18:39-07:00","id":1508314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508147-why-the-world-of-darkness-god-gave-cain-so-much-priviliges?p=1508293#post1508293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It seems then that your disappointment comes from reading too much from one sentence.<br /> <br /> &quot;We're not sure if the story is true and anarch believe it's made up for control&quot; simply speaks of the lacj of definitive proof for the myth of nod, and of the mistrust of anarchs toward it.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, remember that 1st ed corebooks were, at most, sketchbooks of the games. Mage the ascebsuon 1st corebook is basically a wholly different game compared to what mage become following that book.<br /> <br /> So the abarch centrist viewpoint only existed for a few books.<br /> <br /> Also &quot;christians are only x percent of the world&quot;, doesn't matter. Unless you dive too deep in mage's cosmology.<br /> <br /> In all urban fantasy, there's a real truth behind supernaturals being, either as species, like in the WOD, or englobing all of them. And this truth cab align with some real life beliefs. Which means others are wrong.<br /> <br /> And it's not a problem, you don't need to care about every beliefs of the world to creates your urban fantasy worldbuilding.<br /> <br /> Also, VTM doesn't really confirm monotheism. In fact, the whole &quot;testament of Lilith&quot; thing contradicts it.<br /> <br /> All that is certain, is that a god baniqhed a couple from Eden, and Lilith before them, and that he cursed their eldest son for killing his brother.<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> And that's all. The nature of that god is left pretty unknown, and even adding Demon the fallen's lore into all that, the god described, while clearly inspired from the abrahamic god, is pretty different from said god.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for the theme of lies and manipulation through use of myths, it is respected by the fact that, at least since 2nd edition, the camarilla denied the reality of the myrh of Nod because they want to control the younglings.<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> \u200b\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>And how does denying the myth does exactly achieve control? <br /> The story in the book of Nod is a tale of how rebels are punished. First God is cursed for rebelling against God. Later, the Third Generation is cursed by Caine for rebelling against the second. It's a perfect control tool. <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bWhy in hell would Camarilla Elders reject this extremely convenient for them tale?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","name":"Microcuchon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-13T23:18:49-07:00","id":1508329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Microcuchon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508147-why-the-world-of-darkness-god-gave-cain-so-much-priviliges?p=1508314#post1508314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And how does denying the myth does exactly achieve control?<br /> The story in the book of Nod is a tale of how rebels are punished. First God is cursed for rebelling against God. Later, the Third Generation is cursed by Caine for rebelling against the second. It's a perfect control tool.<br /> Why in hell would Camarilla Elders reject this extremely convenient for them tale?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> because knowing the truth of the origin of vampires and the power of the eldest minimise the power of the camarilla.<br /> <br /> If all you know is that the biggest and baddest kindred are those in the inner council of the camarilla, you bend the knee and hopes to never attract their ire, for they are the illuminati and will rule forever.<br /> <br /> But then, if you know that there are blood gods that could crush them and every prince in with a thought (litterally, thanks auspex 8), and that soon, very soon, their awakening will mark the end of known vampire society, the threat of the inner council vanish.<br /> <br /> Why would you care about the claim of praxis of a prince? He's gonna kneel or die before the progenitors as much as you will.<br /> <br /> <br /> As far as most camarilla vampires, and a big portion of anarchs are concerned, the camarilla is indeed the most powerful vampiric power to have ever existed. As such, rebellion is at most a fool's hope.<br /> <br /> But if you know that the story of nod is true, then not only can you see past their pretense, but you may even, in your rebellion, try to wake up antediluvians, which the inner council fear more than anything, for they couldn't stand against such a being.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> <br /> By the way, this isn't a conjecture of mine, I'm basically paraphrasing multiple vtm books, nitably the guide to the camarilla.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bAnd it's also one of the in game argument of sabbat vampires against the camarilla, that they're at best pawn of the eldests, at worse nothing but a sand castle ignoring their inevitable demise.<br /> <br /> As for the myth of nod being about rebels being punished, this is pretty much extrapolating.<br /> <br /> Caine is depicted as the victim of a cosmic injustice, he's a sympathetic protagonist of the text, not a rebel deserving punishment.<br /> <br /> And while he is cursed, he embrace his cursed state, creating a mighty kingdom and a godlike family. If anything, the story is about being prideful and grandiose in one's damnation.<br /> <br /> As for the 13, whule they are all cursed for their paricide, they aren't suffering any more repercussion, caine leaving them to do as they please. In fact, that's exactly what they do next.<br /> If anything, they were better off than most rebels under the camarilla, for which many breaking of traditions ends in final death.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, the story of nod includes the prophecies of gehenna, the inevitable event in which, after many destructions, caine will come back to rule all vampires. This very part is opposed to any pretense of a vampiric authority like the camarilla.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-14T09:18:53-07:00","id":1508362,"title":"","content":"I've never entirely bought the whole &quot;Caine cursing them&quot; anyway. If the weaknesses are Caine's curse, then why do new bloodlines develop their own banes whenever they come into existence? I think a bane is just the side-effect of obsessing so much about a certain lifestyle that the blood calcifies around that obsession, granting the vampire an instinctive ability to develop related disciplines, but also giving them a related weakness.<br /> <br /> Gangrel, for example, obsessing so much over animals that ease with Protean and Animalism became instinctive for her, and her desiring so much to savagely get into brawls without consequence that Fort became instinctive as well. But the side effect was that she developed animal features.<br /> <br /> Then again Nosferatu is hard to explain via that model. So perhaps at least some of them legitimately were cursed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-14T19:02:09-07:00","id":1508407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508147-why-the-world-of-darkness-god-gave-cain-so-much-priviliges?p=1508329#post1508329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> because knowing the truth of the origin of vampires and the power of the eldest minimise the power of the camarilla.<br /> <br /> If all you know is that the biggest and baddest kindred are those in the inner council of the camarilla, you bend the knee and hopes to never attract their ire, for they are the illuminati and will rule forever.<br /> <br /> But then, if you know that there are blood gods that could crush them and every prince in with a thought (litterally, thanks auspex 8), and that soon, very soon, their awakening will mark the end of known vampire society, the threat of the inner council vanish.<br /> <br /> Why would you care about the claim of praxis of a prince? He's gonna kneel or die before the progenitors as much as you will.<br /> <br /> <br /> As far as most camarilla vampires, and a big portion of anarchs are concerned, the camarilla is indeed the most powerful vampiric power to have ever existed. As such, rebellion is at most a fool's hope.<br /> <br /> But if you know that the story of nod is true, then not only can you see past their pretense, but you may even, in your rebellion, try to wake up antediluvians, which the inner council fear more than anything, for they couldn't stand against such a being.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> <br /> By the way, this isn't a conjecture of mine, I'm basically paraphrasing multiple vtm books, nitably the guide to the camarilla.<br /> <br /> <br /> And it's also one of the in game argument of sabbat vampires against the camarilla, that they're at best pawn of the eldests, at worse nothing but a sand castle ignoring their inevitable demise.<br /> <br /> As for the myth of nod being about rebels being punished, this is pretty much extrapolating.<br /> <br /> Caine is depicted as the victim of a cosmic injustice, he's a sympathetic protagonist of the text, not a rebel deserving punishment.<br /> <br /> And while he is cursed, he embrace his cursed state, creating a mighty kingdom and a godlike family. If anything, the story is about being prideful and grandiose in one's damnation.<br /> <br /> As for the 13, whule they are all cursed for their paricide, they aren't suffering any more repercussion, caine leaving them to do as they please. In fact, that's exactly what they do next.<br /> If anything, they were better off than most rebels under the camarilla, for which many breaking of traditions ends in final death.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, the story of nod includes the prophecies of gehenna, the inevitable event in which, after many destructions, caine will come back to rule all vampires. This very part is opposed to any pretense of a vampiric authority like the camarilla.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>That's how they justified it in the source material, but I don't really like it. A power structure needs not only effective power, but also a supporting ideology to endure. <br /> Instead of denying Noddism and persecuting believers, they could have spinned their way, claiming the Inner Circle are the rulers appointed by the Antediluvians while they sleep, and therefore, guardians of the order. That would give them an aura of legitimacy, even if it's a big fat lie. <br /> The fact that Caine let the Antediluvians go after cursing them is irrelevant. The point is that patricide is wrong, not because the Elders of the Camarilla say so, but because the First cursed it. <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","name":"Microcuchon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-14T21:33:33-07:00","id":1508415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508147-why-the-world-of-darkness-god-gave-cain-so-much-priviliges?p=1508251#post1508251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One way to answer this question is to consider that Cain and Abel ( and other persons and beings in the area ) had prior dealings with this spirit being that is referred to as &quot;God&quot; . Hence the attention and actions of this supernatural being towards Cain, and later also interactions with Angels.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>If you go with events from Genesis being literal truth, there wasn't a lot of competition for heavenly attention at the time. Caine was at that point one of what, four living human beings (if Lilith counts), and responsible for that number dropping from its up to that point all-time high of five. Makes sense that with billions of people living, murdering each other, and praying, there might be less focus on each individual in the modern day.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-15T03:54:20-07:00","id":1508427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Microcuchon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508147-why-the-world-of-darkness-god-gave-cain-so-much-priviliges?p=1508407#post1508407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's how they justified it in the source material, but I don't really like it. A power structure needs not only effective power, but also a supporting ideology to endure.<br /> Instead of denying Noddism and persecuting believers, they could have spinned their way, claiming the Inner Circle are the rulers appointed by the Antediluvians while they sleep, and therefore, guardians of the order. That would give them an aura of legitimacy, even if it's a big fat lie.<br /> The fact that Caine let the Antediluvians go after cursing them is irrelevant. The point is that patricide is wrong, not because the Elders of the Camarilla say so, but because the First cursed it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The ideology of the camarilla is already set: a united vampiric society maintaining the masquerade to save the species from another inquisition. It doesn't need more.<br /> <br /> The inner council acknowledging the antediluvian, even to pretend being the overseers of their domain, is already acknowledging a greater power than itself, which opens the door to contesters themselves pretending to be the real agents of the antediluvians. <br /> <br /> And if the history of, say, christianity, teach us anything about multiple people claiming to be the agent of a superior power, is that it cause dissention.<br /> <br /> While denying their existence makes thing simpler. If people claims to be the agents of the antediluvians, the camarilla can roll it's metaphorical eyes while condescendingly mocking these superstitious kids.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for caine punishing his grandchilders, the context is entirely relevant. The camarilla punish murders by final death. Caine merely cursed the third generation. You can't justify your legislation on a father figure that isn't as vehement in the punishment as you.<br /> <br /> <br /> Abd for your exemple of how the council could have spinned the story of Nod, it doesn't works.<br /> <br /> You can't both use the story of the punishment of caine then of the third generation as a warning against the consequence of rebellion AND use them as the source of your authority by claiming to be their legate. That's two irreconciliable positions.<br /> \u200b<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-15T08:09:57-07:00","id":1508446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508147-why-the-world-of-darkness-god-gave-cain-so-much-priviliges?p=1508415#post1508415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you go with events from Genesis being literal truth, there wasn't a lot of competition for heavenly attention at the time. Caine was at that point one of what, four living human beings (if Lilith counts), and responsible for that number dropping from its up to that point all-time high of five. Makes sense that with billions of people living, murdering each other, and praying, there might be less focus on each individual in the modern day.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, the version of Genesis in my Bible (which is an NIV, although I've read other translations) is not so clear cut. Not only does God refer to themselves as multiple while creating the world, but the story of Cain and Abel ends with it being explicitly clear there were other humans (Cain is worried about them killing him, and later has children with a woman from Nod). Genesis has some pretty well known issues with continuity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-16T09:14:54-07:00","id":1508534,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"color:#e74c3c\">A reminder that applies to everyone here to be respectful to posters of all faiths or lack of faith. Its a delicate subject even if it's intrinsic to the game like blood-drinking.</span></b><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-16T10:30:25-07:00","id":1508540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508147-why-the-world-of-darkness-god-gave-cain-so-much-priviliges?p=1508200#post1508200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Cause God in the World of Darkness is an inconsistent messy bitch who is not there to make things better.</div> </div> </div> </div>if you include mage in the world of darkness,that isn't quite true,the celestial chorus believes in kind gentle One. and that One exists,if for one other reason that the CC believe he does.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4621,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","user":"Nicolas Milioni","date":". 04-16-2023, 01:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-16T11:11:35-07:00","id":1508544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508147-why-the-world-of-darkness-god-gave-cain-so-much-priviliges?p=1508540#post1508540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> if you include mage in the world of darkness,that isn't quite true,the celestial chorus believes in kind gentle One. and that One exists,if for one other reason that the CC believe he does.</div> </div> </div> </div>The World of Darkness have large scale entities who's presence and vision act as massive sinks on consensus. The God of Fallen and Masquerade is one such entity, arguably the largest and most powerful of such entities, and it is a certifiable fucking prick. The kind One of the Chrous is not such an entity, and also has all the problems of related monotheistic religions in reality related to it.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Elaborating a bit for clarity, two factors play into this.<br /> <br /> 1) As the original development of World went along and interest started emerging in officially allowing gamelines to operate within each other, the &quot;certain metpahysical actors have more weight on the scales of consensus that others&quot; thing emerged as a sort of answer. &quot;People don't believe in werewolvs modernly&quot; asks one person, &quot;so how can werewolves exist without causing Paradox with their existence&quot;, and the answer to that was &quot;Well, Gaia 'believes' werewolves exist, and Gaia's opinion matters more than any given amount of humanity on the nature of reality.&quot; Basically, Gaia gets to veto humanity's mass belief on account of being the biosphere they live in.<br /> <br /> 2) Demon the Fallen, for better or worse, took that notion and tried to answer and tie everything together by asserting a sort of superpositioned, &quot;all things at once&quot; version reality, where in angels literally dance around AND at the same time background radiation shapes the backdrop of reality, and that the Fall collapsed Schrodinger's reality into consensus dominancy-but the God of Fallen is still the creator of everything in the World of Darkness, and their presence(hell, their absence, as its more likely the case) has an enormous impact on the World of Darkness, even in it's fallen, consensus dominance ridden state. And That God is, in the canon of World, a giant fucking prick, because World was a lot more willing to smack talk Christianity.<br /> <br /> If the One of the Celestial Chorus is somehow not the God of Fallen (and Masquerade, because it seems weird to cut lines that particular way), then it's a construct of consensus, and doesn't have the primacy over reality that the God of Fallen has.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 04-16-2023, 03:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-16T13:35:07-07:00","id":1508558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508147-why-the-world-of-darkness-god-gave-cain-so-much-priviliges?p=1508544#post1508544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The World of Darkness have large scale entities who's presence and vision act as massive sinks on consensus. The God of Fallen and Masquerade is one such entity, arguably the largest and most powerful of such entities, and it is a certifiable fucking prick. The kind One of the Chrous is not such an entity, and also has all the problems of related monotheistic religions in reality related to it.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Elaborating a bit for clarity, two factors play into this.<br /> <br /> 1) As the original development of World went along and interest started emerging in officially allowing gamelines to operate within each other, the &quot;certain metpahysical actors have more weight on the scales of consensus that others&quot; thing emerged as a sort of answer. &quot;People don't believe in werewolvs modernly&quot; asks one person, &quot;so how can werewolves exist without causing Paradox with their existence&quot;, and the answer to that was &quot;Well, Gaia 'believes' werewolves exist, and Gaia's opinion matters more than any given amount of humanity on the nature of reality.&quot; Basically, Gaia gets to veto humanity's mass belief on account of being the biosphere they live in.<br /> <br /> 2) Demon the Fallen, for better or worse, took that notion and tried to answer and tie everything together by asserting a sort of superpositioned, &quot;all things at once&quot; version reality, where in angels literally dance around AND at the same time background radiation shapes the backdrop of reality, and that the Fall collapsed Schrodinger's reality into consensus dominancy-but the God of Fallen is still the creator of everything in the World of Darkness, and their presence(hell, their absence, as its more likely the case) has an enormous impact on the World of Darkness, even in it's fallen, consensus dominance ridden state. And That God is, in the canon of World, a giant fucking prick, because World was a lot more willing to smack talk Christianity.<br /> <br /> If the One of the Celestial Chorus is somehow not the God of Fallen (and Masquerade, because it seems weird to cut lines that particular way), then it's a construct of consensus, and doesn't have the primacy over reality that the God of Fallen has.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I understand your comment better now.<br /> so just so I'm clear, one of the points you are making is that there are beings that are &quot;above the consensus&quot;?<br /> That those beings are so goddamn powerful and strong that they don't give a shit people believe in their existence or not? And thus the Mage rule of &quot;believe define everything&quot; doesn't affect them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4621,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","user":"Nicolas Milioni","date":". 04-16-2023, 04:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-16T13:45:15-07:00","id":1508559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508147-why-the-world-of-darkness-god-gave-cain-so-much-priviliges?p=1508558#post1508558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think I understand your comment better now.<br /> so just so I'm clear, one of the points you are making is that there are beings that are &quot;above the consensus&quot;?<br /> That those beings are so goddamn powerful and strong that they don't give a shit people believe in their existence or not?</div> </div> </div> </div>Somewhat the wrong order of operation, but yes. Fallen's God, Apocalypse's Gaia, and others are effectively massive wills that massively weigh down consensus in certain ways, and Fallen's God in particular has dominancy because Demon the Fallen was intended to tie all the other gamelines together. As that matters to the Celestial Chorus and their One, either a) the many names of God they collect into their One is basically just reinterpretation of Fallen's God, or b) it's a construct of the Chorus's consensus, as opposed to Fallen's God.<br /> <br /> And the God of Fallen is, again, a giant fucking prick-enough nuance you can understand when a demon wants to be a Redeemer, mind, but Time of Judgment's scenario for Fallen is basically God comes back and wipes everything out, rocks fall everyone dies miserably style.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-20T05:25:26-07:00","id":1509028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508147-why-the-world-of-darkness-god-gave-cain-so-much-priviliges?p=1508559#post1508559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the God of Fallen is, again, a giant fucking prick-enough nuance you can understand when a demon wants to be a Redeemer, mind, but Time of Judgment's scenario for Fallen is basically God comes back and wipes everything out, rocks fall everyone dies miserably style.</div> </div> </div> </div>Doesn't time of judgement have 3+ scenarios for demon? Even the One that explicitely deals with heaven(and stats out proper angels) has most of the possibile answers amount to &quot;god left to get cigarettes/milk&quot; or &quot;nietzsche was more right than he knew&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-20T06:19:52-07:00","id":1509031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508147-why-the-world-of-darkness-god-gave-cain-so-much-priviliges?p=1509028#post1509028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Doesn't time of judgement have 3+ scenarios for demon? Even the One that explicitely deals with heaven(and stats out proper angels) has most of the possibile answers amount to &quot;god left to get cigarettes/milk&quot; or <b>&quot;nietzsche was more right than he knew&quot;</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dGDH3meSPyk\" data-code=\"dGDH3meSPyk\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/dGDH3meSPyk/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-20T10:30:22-07:00","id":1509059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508147-why-the-world-of-darkness-god-gave-cain-so-much-priviliges?p=1509028#post1509028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Doesn't time of judgement have 3+ scenarios for demon? Even the One that explicitely deals with heaven(and stats out proper angels) has most of the possibile answers amount to &quot;god left to get cigarettes/milk&quot; or &quot;nietzsche was more right than he knew&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>The point is that there's a range, but the general place Fallen sits at is that it's God is a giant fucking prick.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-20T11:56:48-07:00","id":1509074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508147-why-the-world-of-darkness-god-gave-cain-so-much-priviliges?p=1508427#post1508427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> The ideology of the camarilla is already set: a united vampiric society maintaining the masquerade to save the species from another inquisition. It doesn't need more.<br /> <br /> The inner council acknowledging the antediluvian, even to pretend being the overseers of their domain, is already acknowledging a greater power than itself, which opens the door to contesters themselves pretending to be the real agents of the antediluvians.<br /> <br /> And if the history of, say, christianity, teach us anything about multiple people claiming to be the agent of a superior power, is that it cause dissention.<br /> <br /> While denying their existence makes thing simpler. If people claims to be the agents of the antediluvians, the camarilla can roll it's metaphorical eyes while condescendingly mocking these superstitious kids.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for caine punishing his grandchilders, the context is entirely relevant. The camarilla punish murders by final death. Caine merely cursed the third generation. You can't justify your legislation on a father figure that isn't as vehement in the punishment as you.<br /> <br /> <br /> Abd for your exemple of how the council could have spinned the story of Nod, it doesn't works.<br /> <br /> You can't both use the story of the punishment of caine then of the third generation as a warning against the consequence of rebellion AND use them as the source of your authority by claiming to be their legate. That's two irreconciliable positions.<br /> <br /> \u200b<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Any vampiric organization can maintain the Masquerade. The Anarchs do It; the Followers of Set do it. The Rsvnos do it. Even the Sabbat does it!! <br /> Goverment never have a problem acknowledging a higher power, as long as that power can not refute them. Medieval kings and emperors did it all the time (and the Camarilla elders are from the middle ages). <br /> Dissent is not a consequence of claiming to be the agent of a superior power. Power itself is the consequence. As long as we have power people we will fight for it, and contenders will claim to be legitimate. <br /> Finally, the fact that a story is contradictory doesn't render it impossible to use. <br /> I want to make clear that I don't think lore as written is WRONG, but highlight that other options were possible and I would have preferred them because, IMO, they would have meds more sense thematically<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","name":"Microcuchon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-20T17:27:26-07:00","id":1509118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Microcuchon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508147-why-the-world-of-darkness-god-gave-cain-so-much-priviliges?p=1509074#post1509074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Any vampiric organization can maintain the Masquerade. The Anarchs do It; the Followers of Set do it. The Rsvnos do it. Even the Sabbat does it!!<br /> Goverment never have a problem acknowledging a higher power, as long as that power can not refute them. Medieval kings and emperors did it all the time (and the Camarilla elders are from the middle ages).<br /> Dissent is not a consequence of claiming to be the agent of a superior power. Power itself is the consequence. As long as we have power people we will fight for it, and contenders will claim to be legitimate.<br /> Finally, the fact that a story is contradictory doesn't render it impossible to use.<br /> I want to make clear that I don't think lore as written is WRONG, but highlight that other options were possible and I would have preferred them because, IMO, they would have meds more sense thematically</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> &quot;Any organisation can do X&quot; never stopped organisation from basing their collective identity on asserting that only them and their method is able to achieve a goal.<br /> <br /> The camarilla asserts that only them can maintain the masquerade, and that independant clans need their supervision and that anarch are playing at the masquerade without actually maintaining it.<br /> <br /> Of course it's propaganda, but it's the core of the camarilla's identity.<br /> <br /> <br /> Yes, many civilisations acknowledged higher powers.<br /> Howether, these societies, and their ruling elites, didb't believed that these powers would ever come down to take away the thrones. Nor would communicate to the population outside of priesthood or saints and prophets whose validity was of course decided by the ruling body of religion.<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> The antediluvian, on the other side, are presented as vampires, not faraway deities in heaven but flesh and bones beings as much as younger vampires. With similar desires.<br /> <br /> As such, acknowledging the antediluvian means you acknowledge that there's here, on earth, around 13 beings that have more power than your oganisation could ever dream of possessing, and with the mentality to seek to rule others. <br /> <br /> Which makes your own legitimity shaky, since at any moment, great-great-great-grandaddy can come back and reclail the throne Godfather's style, and since you acknowledged them, any neonates knows that you're nothing but overseer and that any night the real rulers may come back. <br /> In short, you'd paint yourself as a litteral placeholder <br /> <br /> Kings and emperors in history, on the other side, rarely claimed to rule the throne of gods. They were here because the gods allowed it or were chosen for it, and the gods have no interest in coming down to take the throne, since they're not humans and are ruling the cosmos.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> \u200b\u200bI would also add that, after thinking more about it, the idea that the camarilla could have claimed to be the steward of the antediluvians couldn't have possibly worked.<br /> <br /> For two reasons. One, they have in their rank the tremere, whose clanhood was gained by the murder of one of the antediluvian.<br /> Second, three of the four independant clans affirm that their culture and policy directly comes from their own antediluvian. Howether, they are independant, which contradict the claims that antediluvians wants<br /> a common society of vampire.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> You could brush it off by making the camarilla claim that only some antediluvians are for the camarilla, and that they are the keepers of their thrones.<br /> <br /> Howether, that shatters their claim of authority on all kindred, since now they only rules for the antediluvians of the camarilla clans, and have no legitimacy on, say, camarilla setites, ravnos, tzimisce or assamites.<br /> It also negates all hope of one day ruling other tzimisce and lasombra,. Since the clans based their modern culture on the deliberate murder of their progenitor. Who are the camarilla to claim to rule us for a vampire that we killed?<br /> <br /> <br /> The only logical solution is for the camarilla to claim to rule for the species common good, which, being an ideal, is a call to legitimacy far more solid than &quot;these beings said we rule&quot;<br /> Especially since said beings could at any instant come out of their nap and say &quot;bullshit&quot;.<br /> <br /> &quot;Rule by antediluvian right&quot; is a far too shaky foundation for a group that hopes to rule forever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-20T23:50:05-07:00","id":1509139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508147-why-the-world-of-darkness-god-gave-cain-so-much-priviliges?p=1508362#post1508362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Then again Nosferatu is hard to explain via that model. So perhaps at least some of them legitimately were cursed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I not entirely right, but I read somewhere that nosferatu antidilluvian cursed his our children because he hated then and that him not have the curse, maybe this could even be a start for a history.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-21T00:35:10-07:00","id":1509144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508147-why-the-world-of-darkness-god-gave-cain-so-much-priviliges?p=1508362#post1508362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've never entirely bought the whole &quot;Caine cursing them&quot; anyway. If the weaknesses are Caine's curse, then why do new bloodlines develop their own banes whenever they come into existence? I think a bane is just the side-effect of obsessing so much about a certain lifestyle that the blood calcifies around that obsession, granting the vampire an instinctive ability to develop related disciplines, but also giving them a related weakness.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think each of these Bloodlines weaknesses are more unexpected or unintended consequences of their creations if you think about it would make sense.<br /> <br /> Samedi: They originated from an experiment involving the blood of vampires and his weakness is a consequence of this artificial creation, an imperfect experiment if you will.<br /> <br /> Lhiannan: Hard to say, it seems they draw their power from somewhere which generates a source that is limited, so they lose a generation every time they embrace.<br /> <br /> Ahrimanes: Created from Verbenna rituals, supposedly, and its weakness is a planned consequence, not to leave a new race of vampires without a curse to spread.<br /> <br /> Kiasyd: Result of individual adaptation or a consequence of lineage consuming faerie blood or being exposed to glamour, something along those lines.<br /> <br /> Sirens: Their origin is unclear so it's hard to say, but you might think it's like a congenital defect or a way for the eldest of the bloodline to control the younger ones, kind of like Malkav might do with his clan.<br /> <br /> There are other Bloodlines, but I think you get the idea.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-21T09:43:33-07:00","id":1509202,"title":"","content":"Or Old Clan Tzismce who disdain for flesh crafting resulted in them not having the ability as an adaptation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-21T23:43:16-07:00","id":1509258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508147-why-the-world-of-darkness-god-gave-cain-so-much-priviliges?p=1509118#post1509118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Any organisation can do X&quot; never stopped organisation from basing their collective identity on asserting that only them and their method is able to achieve a goal.<br /> <br /> The camarilla asserts that only them can maintain the masquerade, and that independant clans need their supervision and that anarch are playing at the masquerade without actually maintaining it.<br /> <br /> Of course it's propaganda, but it's the core of the camarilla's identity.<br /> <br /> <br /> Yes, many civilisations acknowledged higher powers.<br /> Howether, these societies, and their ruling elites, didb't believed that these powers would ever come down to take away the thrones. Nor would communicate to the population outside of priesthood or saints and prophets whose validity was of course decided by the ruling body of religion.<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> The antediluvian, on the other side, are presented as vampires, not faraway deities in heaven but flesh and bones beings as much as younger vampires. With similar desires.<br /> <br /> As such, acknowledging the antediluvian means you acknowledge that there's here, on earth, around 13 beings that have more power than your oganisation could ever dream of possessing, and with the mentality to seek to rule others.<br /> <br /> Which makes your own legitimity shaky, since at any moment, great-great-great-grandaddy can come back and reclail the throne Godfather's style, and since you acknowledged them, any neonates knows that you're nothing but overseer and that any night the real rulers may come back.<br /> In short, you'd paint yourself as a litteral placeholder<br /> <br /> Kings and emperors in history, on the other side, rarely claimed to rule the throne of gods. They were here because the gods allowed it or were chosen for it, and the gods have no interest in coming down to take the throne, since they're not humans and are ruling the cosmos.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> \u200b\u200bI would also add that, after thinking more about it, the idea that the camarilla could have claimed to be the steward of the antediluvians couldn't have possibly worked.<br /> <br /> For two reasons. One, they have in their rank the tremere, whose clanhood was gained by the murder of one of the antediluvian.<br /> Second, three of the four independant clans affirm that their culture and policy directly comes from their own antediluvian. Howether, they are independant, which contradict the claims that antediluvians wants<br /> a common society of vampire.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> You could brush it off by making the camarilla claim that only some antediluvians are for the camarilla, and that they are the keepers of their thrones.<br /> <br /> Howether, that shatters their claim of authority on all kindred, since now they only rules for the antediluvians of the camarilla clans, and have no legitimacy on, say, camarilla setites, ravnos, tzimisce or assamites.<br /> It also negates all hope of one day ruling other tzimisce and lasombra,. Since the clans based their modern culture on the deliberate murder of their progenitor. Who are the camarilla to claim to rule us for a vampire that we killed?<br /> <br /> <br /> The only logical solution is for the camarilla to claim to rule for the species common good, which, being an ideal, is a call to legitimacy far more solid than &quot;these beings said we rule&quot;<br /> Especially since said beings could at any instant come out of their nap and say &quot;bullshit&quot;.<br /> <br /> &quot;Rule by antediluvian right&quot; is a far too shaky foundation for a group that hopes to rule forever.</div> </div> </div> </div>My explanation may not be perfect, but yours also have some logical flaws.<br /> To start with, ancient peoples DID believe their gods were real and ruled their lives and Christians actually believed God would eventually come down from Heaven and claim His Throne in the Kingdom. That never stopped them from claiming Divine Right.<br /> <br /> Secondly, if the Antediluvians ever came to take power directly, it wouldn't matter how the Camarilla justified their power before, because they would be obliterated as a power structure regardless.<br /> Actually, if they had been claiming to have been ruling in the Antediluvians stead at least they would have left some manouvering room open. Now imagine that you have ruled for centuries denying someone exists and suddenly this someone turns up. Not only have to painted yourself as a lier but also pissed off the big guy, whose authority you have been denying.<br /> <br /> The Tremere situation is definitely problematic, but it can always be spinned as Saulot was mad and had to go. The independent are not, you can claim they are lying and massively gaslight them: &quot;So Set said you should be independent? Great, ask Set to come and tell me so..&quot; And yes, I know this is a game the Camarilla's enemies can also play. As always, belief and power are intertwined.<br /> <br /> So no, there is no ONLY LOGICAL SOLUTION.Justification of power is never logical as power is just an imposition of strength over others. There will always be cracks in the argument.<br /> <br /> And finally, an interesting point. The Camarilla doesn't intend to rule FOREVER because any Vampire clever enough to have lived for a few centuries has already realized that the first rule of History is &quot;NOTHING LASTS FOREVER&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27429,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","user":"Microcuchon","date":". 04-22-2023, 02:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","name":"Microcuchon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-23T10:30:11-07:00","id":1509396,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m pleased that we kept this debate civil so far.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-23T20:07:43-07:00","id":1509435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Conradine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508147-why-the-world-of-darkness-god-gave-cain-so-much-priviliges#post1508147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the WoD main story, Cain murdered his own brother and is utterly unrepentant about it. God offers him every occasion to repent, even giving him eternal life and sending three ( or four according to the Golconda legend ) angels to offer him forgiveness.<br /> <br /> A common vampire Embraced against his will, who's worse sins were lying to his wife and cursing after a disliked politician, can pray and beg and cry and repent as much as he wants but 99% of time Heaven stay absolutely silent to his prayers and no angel is there to offer any kind of salvation.<br /> <br /> So...<br /> why?</div> </div> </div> </div>The most basic idea is that God intended to punish Cain for committing murder by turning Caine into a vampire, but that's only one possibility.<br /> <br /> I recall the Malkavian clanbook, in which a Malkavian recounted the Caine/Abel story but then suggested that Caine's vampirism was actually intended to be a <i>blessing</i> from God. Caine realized the &quot;trick&quot; that that God likes blood sacrifices, understood that human blood was more powerful than vampire blood, so he killed Abel, spilling his brother's blood as a sacrifice to God. God was pleased that Caine had come to such a realization and so God rewarded Caine by turning him into a vampire.<br /> <br /> In such a case, the idea that Caine was punished was an idea that was created by humans (who, understandably, aren't too thrilled at the idea that God enjoys seeing them sacrificed on alters), and that idea ended up percolating through Vampire society as well. So these days many vampires view vampirism as a curse, because they view the first vampire as cursed. But if God intended Caine's condition as a blessing, then stories about God sending angels to give Caine a chance at &quot;forgiveness&quot; aren't true, and it also explains why regular vampires aren't ever offered &quot;forgiveness.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 04-23-2023, 11:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-23T20:20:48-07:00","id":1509437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508147-why-the-world-of-darkness-god-gave-cain-so-much-priviliges?p=1509118#post1509118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could brush it off by making the camarilla claim that only some antediluvians are for the camarilla, and that they are the keepers of their thrones.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I've always taken the Camarilla's official position to be that there are Clan Founders, but they're not Antidelluvians - ancient blood gods who predate the Biblical flood. The clan founders, if any of them still exist, are powerful vampires, but that's it. They're not all powerful gods and they're hardly all knowing. They can be killed and have been killed. There are quite a few clans out there whose clan founders have been killed within recent vampire memory. <br /> <br /> If a clan founder ever did woke up, they'd be more terrified of television and automobiles than you should be of them. They'd probably eventually assume a position of some regional authority once they came to terms with the modern world, but they're not going to be controlling the world. Look at Cappadocius and Lasombra - both of them were active only 500 years ago, and neither of them controlled the entire world, or anything close to it, and they both ended up getting killed because they were anything but all powerful or all knowing. Why would anybody think that if some other clan founders work up today that they'd be all powerful blood gods unlike those two? <br /> <br /> Of course, with the awakening of Ravnos that changes the math a bit, but I imagine the Camarilla would generally brush it off as some sort of Ravnos prank, or some sort of mystic thaumaturgy rather than due to the personal power of a clan founder. Because if Ravnos was that strong, how come none of the other clan founders were?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-23T23:42:08-07:00","id":1509455,"title":"","content":"Even if you don't abide by any particular fictional vampire take on Noddist myth, the Bible itself has Cain both punished and protected: he committed a grievous sin, but before divine moral laws had been communicated to humanity. Cain was banished, but plead for some mercy, and was granted it in the form of the Mark of Cain, a symbol by which all would know inherently that to bring harm to Cain would curse themselves and their families for interrupting with Cain's divine punishment. The Hebrew word translated as &quot;mark&quot; is also used to describe the rainbow signaling the end of The Flood, and the the Plagues Upon Egypt: unmistakable signs of divine wrath, but also glimmers of hope for at least some people.<br /> <br /> It's not all the difficult to translate the &quot;our world but darker&quot; concept with the well tread idea that the Creator is a complete asshole in the WoD, into the idea that Caine received a &quot;mixed blessing&quot; rather than one blessing and one punishment, in order to ensure Caine's eternal suffering for his crimes (there's three of them technically, the second, which has interesting things to toy with in Noddist myth, is that Caine force the Earth to drink Abel's blood, despoiling the land, and the third of lying about it which actually got the biggest response even in the original telling of the story). The idea that vampires are trapped in a state that forces them to acknowledge they are gifted and damned, and their mythology seeks to address that, while humans get a version that's more black &amp; white over matters","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-26T05:58:58-07:00","id":1509708,"title":"","content":"<i>First let me say a few things as a preface</i>: I generally ascribe to One World of Darkness, and assign hierarchy (as in, which takes precedent if another disagrees) on the settings in, usually, this order Mage &gt; Kindred of the East = Werewolf &gt; Demon = Hunter &gt; Wraith &gt; Vampire &gt; Changeling; (The Reason that vampire and changeling are so low is, vampire is concerned with a very static manipulative subset so lies are par of the course and Changeling is literally retconnable in universe). Finally I go by literal interpretations wherever I can - I generally love the metaplot. Oh, and this does not concern V5, as that has disregarded most of it [In general, I approach V5 same as Requiem: Generally reused names, Fundamentally different game].<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Headcanon</b>: It wasn't god who cursed Caine. It was, Adam, his father. It's quite clear that the firstborn had really insane abilities (see Lilith telling God to go f* himself, Eve controlling the Underworld as the lady of fate, etc). The Curse is born of Adam's guilt on ordering Caine to make the sacrifice (and setting into motion the Death of his then youngest son).<br /> <br /> Seriously, read the passage in the Book of Nod. Adam is always called Father, and god is always called the One Above. And the verse where the curse is described says:<br /> <br /> <i>But my Father said<br /> &quot;Cursed are you Caine,<br /> who killed your brother.<br /> As I was cast out,<br /> so shall you be&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Now Lilith, the original rebel before Lucifer made it cool, teaches Caine how to circumvent parts of his father's curse (which effectively distances him from his heritage) and access his higher nature (his avatar) - what Lilith tries here is to make him like her, to deify him. So, he enters a seeking (he was never really a Sleeper, that wasn't a thing back then) and his higher self begins showing its power.<br /> <br /> Now, what about the angels? Well, remember than the first murder turned the war in heaven bloody. Then the psycho bastard who made murder suddenly begins exhibiting divine powers. The Angels cursing Caine are probably trying to get him to repent, to <i>undo</i> the creation of murder, to supplicate himself to the One instead of becoming a threat. Keep in mind that the Elohim don't understand Awakened wills very well, especially the loyalists - what Abel's murder was, was a spell adding a new law into the world (Murder is Possible). Oh, and Gabriel offers Golconda instead of what others did because out of the Loyalists he is the most rebellious - there's a passage in demon which has him potentially fall because he refuses to leave a siege (under orders from the One) in defense of a single human. Gabriel actively assists the Seeking, while the others try to impede.<br /> <br /> Then Caine comes back from the Seeking, understanding his powers, and Lilith asks him to stop pushing so hard because he is going to break himself. Aaand he doesn't listen, open himself up to the Night (keep in mind, Night here can mean really dark things) and comes into contact with a manifestation of the Wyrm (Beast of War) which gives him power, but also gives him a Beast - and thus solidifies the taint of the curse. <br /> <br /> <b>So back to the subject at hand</b>, why is the curse so punitive to others? Because Caine isn't just a product of the curse. He was offered partial freedom through Lilith and, more importantly, <b>he never died.</b> Caine isn't a vampire. Enoch is the first vampire. Caine is the dark Father, he is a Tainted, Cursed <i>something</i> but he <i>does</i> have an avatar and thus quite a say so on his own limitations. The rest are spiritually mutilated shadows of who they were, whose higher selves have been replaced by a piece of the Beast of War. <i>Of course</i> the curse sucks so much for them.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12911-lateral-psychotropy","name":"Lateral.Psychotropy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-27T14:58:55-07:00","id":1509896,"title":"","content":"The only thing we can say for sure is that &quot;Caine&quot; spun a story to his childer &amp; grandchilder and they wouldn't be able to confirm it as truth or a lie and had to accept as they were not there. Plus who knows what ancients like Yima &amp; Ur-Shurgi were told by there elders.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-28T07:12:23-07:00","id":1509956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lateral.Psychotropy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508147-why-the-world-of-darkness-god-gave-cain-so-much-priviliges?p=1509708#post1509708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>First let me say a few things as a preface</i>: I generally ascribe to One World of Darkness, and assign hierarchy (as in, which takes precedent if another disagrees) on the settings in, usually, this order </div> </div> </div> </div>Why do you place some types of magical persons and supernatural beings as definitely having more knowledge and being more intelligent, in regard to truths, topics, events, and facts considered and regarded as mystical or important ? Do you have clear and exact reasons in regard to the particular organizations, teams, and groups you mentioned ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-28T20:47:30-07:00","id":1510023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508147-why-the-world-of-darkness-god-gave-cain-so-much-priviliges?p=1509956#post1509956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why do you place some types of magical persons and supernatural beings as definitely having more knowledge and being more intelligent, in regard to truths, topics, events, and facts considered and regarded as mystical or important ? Do you have clear and exact reasons in regard to the particular organizations, teams, and groups you mentioned ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Clear and exact reasons? No, this is WoD, there's nothing clear and exact about it. But I have some reasons of a more intuitive nature, and I have some mostly thematic - and of course it is also an aesthetic choice, of what convinces me and what doesn't.<br /> <br /> A pretty important part has to do with breadth of capability (what they <b>can</b> do, and do relatively easily) combined with a push towards learning about everything that isn't just them (effectively, how much each of these groups is pushed to understand the world). You can read on, but I doubt I have what you want; still, I appreciate the question:<br /> <br /> Out of all these, Mage is the most expansive in capability and understanding - it's the only splat that is literally capable of <b>making</b> every other, going <b>everywhere</b>, and at the same time pushed towards learning and understanding. Werewolf goes next because of how expansive the reach of most werewolves is (their connection to the spirit world alone alows them so much knowledge the others don't have), coupled with things like the Mokole and Mnesis. Kindred of the East I mostly put second for a metatextual reason - it was whitewolf's first attempt for a semi unified cosmology.<br /> <br /> Demon and Hunter are two sides of the same coin, and their information comes from similar (if antithetical) sources. They have access of a lot of knowldge, or they interact a lot with other hidden aspects of the world, but their perspectives are <b>so biased</b> as to make them very very difficult to use. Wraith is where it is because it's extremely limited in scope. 2/3rds of the spirits worlds are completely out, plus the material world is somewhat remote - wraiths know a lot about the underworld, and I trust in what they know, but they just focus on that.<br /> <br /> Vampire are neither particularly introspective or particularly interested in anything other than themselves so they are not very good at describing the mysteries of the world. And finally, the grand exception: Changeling <b>would</b> be extremly good at it, but Changeling is literally the setting of <i>actively forgetting and rewriting your lore</i>. Maybe Dark Ages: Fae might apply though, haven't included that.<br /> <br /> Hence, Mage &gt; Kindred of the East = Werewolf &gt; Demon = Hunter &gt; Wraith &gt; Vampire &gt; Changeling; I absolutely get switching some of these. Some might put KotE first, others Demon. I just think that Mage is the one that needs the least effort to describe all of the others without conflict, so I put it first, but Changeling can do the same, for instance, just with a lot more clarity.<br /> <br /> PS: Also I love the Bahari, so I admit my absolute bias for all Lilith related stuff :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12911-lateral-psychotropy","name":"Lateral.Psychotropy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-29T15:17:11-07:00","id":1510129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lateral.Psychotropy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508147-why-the-world-of-darkness-god-gave-cain-so-much-priviliges?p=1510023#post1510023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Clear and exact reasons? No, this is WoD, there's nothing clear and exact about it. But I have some reasons of a more intuitive nature, and I have some mostly thematic - and of course it is also an aesthetic choice, of what convinces me and what doesn't.<br /> <br /> A pretty important part has to do with breadth of capability (what they <b>can</b> do, and do relatively easily) combined with a push towards learning about everything that isn't just them (effectively, how much each of these groups is pushed to understand the world). You can read on, but I doubt I have what you want; still, I appreciate the question:<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> Thank you for this answer / post, it is definitely great, nice, and good to see and read a normal and positive analysis, opinion and summary that includes the varied and different magical beings and supernatural persons from the mysterious, fantastical, good, and positive World of Darkness publications, manuals, books, and novels.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lateral.Psychotropy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508147-why-the-world-of-darkness-god-gave-cain-so-much-priviliges?p=1510023#post1510023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> PS: Also I love the Bahari, so I admit my absolute bias for all Lilith related stuff :P</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you point to / indicate novels and books where Mistress Lilith is mentioned and described ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-29T21:43:21-07:00","id":1510159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508147-why-the-world-of-darkness-god-gave-cain-so-much-priviliges?p=1510129#post1510129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could you point to / indicate novels and books where Mistress Lilith is mentioned and described ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the biggest one is Revelations of the Dark Mother. She makes an appearance is most of the major in-game books (Both book of Nod and Erciyes Fragments have a chapter on her, I seem to remember something in Days of Fire too, but I am unsure). Mage has some refferences on her in the Book of the Fallen (Because Lilith is considered the first Qliphoth, but the book says that it's not actually her and associates her with <b>another</b> qliphoth) and, I think, there's also a refference about some Djinn following her in Gods and Monsters. Gehena also has some scenarios with Lilith, but they kinda suck.<br /> <br /> Other than that, there are a lot of small mentions: in dark ages where the lamia bloodline is concerned, the Verbena tradition in mage consider her one of the Aeduna, Changelings think she turned changelings into the first vampires (I doubt that, but she is correlated with vampires so it's an easy mistake), in Clanbook: gangrel (one of the myths is that Ennoia, the Gangrel Antediluvian, is Liliths daughter) and I remembered that there was something in Clanbook: Giovanni about her, but I can't find it so I might be misremembering.<br /> <br /> But, in general, if you want to know about Lilith, Revelations of the Dark Mother is the way to go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12911-lateral-psychotropy","name":"Lateral.Psychotropy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-30T10:59:17-07:00","id":1510217,"title":"","content":"\u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lateral.Psychotropy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508147-why-the-world-of-darkness-god-gave-cain-so-much-priviliges?p=1510159#post1510159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, the biggest one is Revelations of the Dark Mother. She makes an appearance is most of the major in-game books (Both book of Nod and Erciyes Fragments have a chapter on her, I seem to remember something in Days of Fire too, but I am unsure). Mage has some refferences on her in the Book of the Fallen (Because Lilith is considered the first Qliphoth, but the book says that it's not actually her and associates her with another qliphoth) and, I think, there's also a refference about some Djinn following her in Gods and Monsters. Gehena also has some scenarios with Lilith, but they kinda suck.<br /> <br /> Other than that, there are a lot of small mentions: in dark ages where the lamia bloodline is concerned, the Verbena tradition in mage consider her one of the Aeduna, Changelings think she turned changelings into the first vampires (I doubt that, but she is correlated with vampires so it's an easy mistake), in Clanbook: gangrel (one of the myths is that Ennoia, the Gangrel Antediluvian, is Liliths daughter) and I remembered that there was something in Clanbook: Giovanni about her, but I can't find it so I might be misremembering.<br /> <br /> But, in general, if you want to know about Lilith, Revelations of the Dark Mother is the way to go.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for the details and information about Mistress Lilith. Certainly I will read and consider these particular sections, chapters, and paragraphs.<br /> Mistress Lilith is one of my favourite characters in the World of Darkness. I seriously like her themes, ideas, concepts, descriptions, and portrayal.\u200b<br /> <br /> Here are some illustrations and pictures related to Mistress Lilith.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <img title=\"image.png\" data-tempid=\"temp_1193_1682877498726_443\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1193\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1193\" data-thumb-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1193&amp;type=thumb\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"image.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-need-data-att-update js-lightbox-participant\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <br /> <img title=\"image.png\" data-tempid=\"temp_1194_1682877512277_46\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\"